sd(3), virtio-blk(3), fs(4), manifest(6)

# BUGS

What the disk holds lasts as long as the service: a reboot, or the service's restart, gives an empty disk.
A disk starts empty, so it has no partitions until something writes a partition table, and it reads that only when it starts (sd(3)).
